  "result": "Done! I've implemented voucher support:\n\n**Updated src/errors.js:**\n- Added VOUCHER_EXISTS \u2014 \"Invoice already has a voucher\"\n\n**Added applyVoucher to src/invoices.js:**\n- `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` \u2014 applies a fixed-amount voucher to a draft invoice\n  - Validates amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Only works on draft invoices (NOT_DRAFT)\n  - Prevents multiple vouchers per invoice (VOUCHER_EXISTS)\n  - Stores voucher as `{ code, amount }`\n  - Never mutates input\n\n**Updated invoiceTotals:**\n- Now returns `voucher` field (amount, 0 if no voucher)\n- Calculates total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher\n- Clamps total at 0 (can't go negative even with oversized voucher)\n\n**Tests:**\n- Updated existing invoiceTotals tests to check voucher field\n- Added 9 new test cases covering:\n  - Applying voucher to draft invoices\n  - Validation (type, sign, non-negative)\n  - Draft-only restriction\n  - One-voucher-per-invoice limit\n  - Non-mutation guarantee\n  - Correct total calculation with voucher\n  - Clamping behavior when voucher > remaining balance\n- All 156 tests pass\n\n**Design:**\n- Vouchers apply AFTER VAT (reduce the final invoice amount)\n- One voucher per invoice (can't stack multiple)\n- Fixed amount in cents (not a percentage)\n- Can't apply to issued/paid invoices (draft only)\n- Total is clamped at 0 even if voucher exceeds amount owed",
